{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 7ba23ed9662d85a4c1170f2b9805a6afbd58724d (tree 31202cbca440d77d3550dde4d916fd55436f436d), BO1-W1 step 1 with the two notes corrected, on published c02f76a0. The verdict binds the structural implementation promise b8d7bd6c (request 55b67149) and signs all seven path artifacts, with the 1a6f7324 artifact first. It carries my approval 22a1eb71 of c61b5c4b forward and authorizes no deploy. The planner lands and deploys.\n\n## The delta\n`git diff c61b5c4b 7ba23ed9` changes two notes and nothing else (`git diff --name-only c61b5c4b 7ba23ed9 -- apps packages scripts docs` is empty), so the configuration, test, security documents and machine inventory are byte-identical to c61b5c4b. The source is the gated source of 8a9bcfc6, and the gate evidence I verified in aaeb0842 stands (END c6acb343).\n- **Plan note, Configuration.** \"The first step removes the Start setting\" becomes \"removed\", and the `DEMO_START_CONFIG` item is in the past tense: Step 1 removed it, it held a string `register: \"unplanned\"`, `demoCreationConfig` requires a full `{scope, genesis}` reference, the setting also enabled the Page Start link, and a later Start setup needs its own reviewed reference and open-policy decision. Every reason is kept, as planner act 7b49f45b asked. The config at this head has no such key, so the line is true at landing.\n- **Plan note, timed step.** \"The checker stays available for the timed review\" becomes \"The checker offers best-effort availability. Before signing, the planner asks the checker in the workroom and by message, then waits for a reply.\" That matches the non-blocking point I made in afb4a745. The 8-minute approval and 10-minute deploy stops and the line that these limits do not guarantee completion are unchanged.\n- **Structure note.** The second \"review head\" sentence now reads \"The configuration and test at gated head `8a9bcfc6` match those at the review head byte-for-byte\", which names each head once, as I asked in 22a1eb71.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The seven filed artifacts equal the seven changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only c02f76a0 7ba23ed9`): the Worker config, the CLI test, three security documents and the two notes. None is missing, extra or twice.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main is clean with tree 31202cbc. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 4 commits, `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path.\n- **Gate.** The delta is two notes, so the gate stands.\n\n## Wake rate\nNotes only on this delta. No alarm, retry or reschedule is added, so the wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged. The closed-state deploy adds a Worker with an idle baseline, which the plan note bounds at 25 requests in a 15-minute window before Hugh's block.\n\n## Architecture\nThe plan and the structure note now agree with the head: Step 1 is past tense, the gated head is named once, and the timed step asks for the checker instead of assuming one.\n\n## Security\nNotes only. No source, token, header or custody path changes, and the notes hold no secret. My conclusions in aaeb0842 and 22a1eb71 stand.\n\n## Simplification\nNothing to remove.\n\n## Non-blocking\nThe wind-down order (planner act c5903c15) says the timed founding does not start. The note's \"best-effort availability\" sentence therefore applies to a later session. The planner will ask the checker by message before signing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1a6f732462ad55827dbf5eaaa551c691c8ac4554","binding":"assigned","head":"7ba23ed9662d85a4c1170f2b9805a6afbd58724d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e8e23a5fbf5af39172f3d9d30bce47a242ad76fe\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b8d7bd6cc04987a5eaac496925c70f22abb2f36f\"]","review_frontier":"